# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — project catalog

This folder groups every repository of the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** project. It is not a
git repository itself; each child folder is.

- **`{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context/`** is the project's knowledge base and its Claude Code
  marketplace. Read its `CLAUDE.md` and `docs/README.md` before making a claim about
  the project's scope, decisions, vocabulary or ownership.
- Every other folder is a code repository. Each enables the shared plugin
  `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared@{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context` in its own `.claude/settings.json`;
  `/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared:{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context` is the entry point to the
  knowledge base from inside any of them.

## Decision records belong to the context repository

**Every decision record for this project is written to
`{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context/docs/decisions/`, never into a code repository** — one folder,
one number sequence, one index, whichever repository the discussion happened in.

Record one with `/tsh-core:managing-decision-records` and give it that folder as the
archive location; the record format, the status vocabulary and the index schema are
that skill's, and `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context/conventions/decisions.md` matches them. From
a code repository the path is `../{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context/docs/decisions/`; from this
folder it is `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context/docs/decisions/`.

A code repository may keep records about **itself** — its own internal conventions — in
its own archive. Anything another repository or another role would need to know goes to
the context repository.

This file loads in every Claude Code session started in a folder below it. Keep it to
pointers; the rules themselves live in `{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-context/CLAUDE.md`.
